# Why: Signing transport selection (local cert vs Google Cloud HSM), contact
#      info embedded in every PAdES signature, and the cert cache itself must
#      all consult the BizRethink `BizrethinkInstanceSigningConfig` singleton
#      row BEFORE falling back to env vars. This lets operators hot-swap
#      signing certs, TSA URLs, and contact info via the admin UI
#      (/admin/instance-signing) without a Coolify redeploy.
#
#      CRYPTOGRAPHICALLY CRITICAL surface. The signing transport produced
#      by `getSigner()` is what writes the PAdES signature into every
#      sealed PDF — if the wrong cert is selected (or env-only fallback
#      kicks in when DB config exists), contracts get signed with the
#      wrong cryptographic key, invalidating their legal standing.
#
#      Three integration points in this file:
#
#        1. `getSigner()` (lines 27-42) — DB-first transport selection.
#           Calls `getInstanceSigningConfig()` (dynamic import to avoid
#           circular dep); if a DB row exists, builds the local-cert or
#           GCP-HSM transport from DB values; otherwise falls back to
#           upstream's env-based factory.
#
#        2. `resetSigningCaches()` (lines 57-64) — NEW export. The admin
#           UI's "Save signing config" handler calls this after writing
#           the new config row so the next `signPdf()` call picks up
#           the change. Without it, signing config would only take
#           effect on next process restart.
#
#        3. `signPdf()` contact-info resolution (lines 71-79) — embeds
#           the contact info string into every PAdES signature dictionary.
#           Reads DB config first (so admins can set "BizRethink AI
#           Compliance <legal@bizrethink.ai>" or similar) with env-var
#           fallback.
#
